  m_text: Mirrors and highly reflective surfaces cause severe laser scattering and
    false depth readings. The scanner may interpret the reflection as a continuation
    of the room, creating 'ghost' geometry and corrupting the point cloud. Mirrors
    must be covered or treated with scanning spray before capturing.
