  m_text: Large, plain white walls lack the visual reference points required by the
    SLAM algorithm. Scanning homogeneous surfaces can cause the device to lose spatial
    awareness, leading to overlapping geometry or tracking drift. It is recommended
    to use artificial scanning targets or add temporary visual markers.
